  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have a keyboard with four special keys:\n\n\nPrint 'A': Prints a single 'A' on the screen\nCtrl-A: Selects everything on the screen\nCtrl-C: Copies the selection to buffer\nCtrl-V: Pastes the buffer content after existing content\nGiven NNN keystrokes, find the maximum number of 'A's that can be displayed on the screen.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line contains TTT - number of test cases\nEach test case consists of:\n\nSingle line containing an integer NNN - number of keystrokes allowed\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case:\n\nPrint a single integer - maximum number of 'A's possible",
    "constraints": [
      "1 &lt;= N &lt;= 50"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n7\n4\n5",
        "output": "3\n9\n4\n5",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 (N=3):\n\nOptimal sequence: A, A, A\nResult: 3 A's\n\nTest Case 2 (N=7):\n\nOptimal sequence: A, A, A, Ctrl-A, Ctrl-C, Ctrl-V, Ctrl-V\nInitial: AAA\nAfter Ctrl-A, Ctrl-C: AAA (selected and copied)\nAfter first Ctrl-V: AAAAAA\nAfter second Ctrl-V: AAAAAAAAA\nResult: 9 A's"
      }
    ]
  },
